body:
Sorry for the delay. It's not something that was easy to reproduce, I ended up fixing it in my end and haven't had it crash anymore.

I believe in the loop when the element was removed it (the iterator) could be invalidated.
` transition_groups.erase(it->key); `

Then at the end of the loop, we try to iterate to the next element in the hashmap, but that iterator isn't valid anymore, so we end up with undefined behavior leading to the crash.

The line that the stack trace is pointing to:
`Control *node = ObjectDB::get_instance(it->key.first);`

Is the next loop, where we're trying to use the invalid iterator.

```cpp
void StyleBox::redraw_animating_nodes() {
	for (HashMap<AnimKey, AnimationState>::Iterator it = transition_groups.begin(); it;) {
		HashMap<AnimKey, AnimationState>::Iterator next = it;
		++next; // Here we're saving a reference to the iterator and advancing it before we end up invalidating the current one

		Control *node = ObjectDB::get_instance<Control>(it->key.first);
		if (node) {
			if (it->value.current_time < it->value.end_time) {
				node->queue_redraw();
			} else if (it->value.end_time > 0) {
				// Draw one extra frame for finished exit animations.
				// Ensures the final state does not draw the final frame of the stylebox at all.
				if (it->value.is_exiting) {
					transition_groups.erase(it->key); // Here when we erase the current element, we still have the next one safe in another variable.
					node->queue_redraw();
				}
			} else {
				// Just a way to detect if an animation JUST finished or any frame after.
				it->value.end_time = 0;
			}
		} else {
			transition_groups.erase(it->key);
		}
		it = next; // Here instead of iterating on a potential invalid iterator, we instead set it with our safe reference we saved before.
	}
}
```

This solved the crash for me.

- Edit -
Love the PR by the way, thank you for it :) It's been super useful, a lot of tweens I used to use in code to animate my buttons were replaced now by the easy to setup stylebox animations in the inspector.
